	(footprint "pluto_rx2_8way:USB_C_Receptacle_HRO_TYPE-C-31-M-12A"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "72c0290f-c7d6-4b05-baf5-22add446305e")
		(at 46 88.81)
		(descr "USB Type-C 2.0 receptacle, HRO TYPE-C-31-M-12A (LCSC C5337088): 16 contacts on 12 SMT lands + 4 PTH shell legs + 2 NPTH alignment holes. AUTHORED FROM THE VENDOR SHEET - THIS IS NOT THE KiCad STOCK PART AND MUST NOT BE SWAPPED BACK FOR IT. Source: HRO drawing TYPE-C-31-M-12A REV A, 2022.10.26 (sha256 fd8a23ee..., committed at 02_parts/TYPE-C-31-M-12A/), view 'RECOMMEND P.C.B LAYOUT (COMPONENT SIDE)', whose own note reads 'TOLERANCE FOR PCB LAYOUT IS +/-0.05'. WHY IT EXISTS: Connector_USB:USB_C_Receptacle_HRO_TYPE-C-31-M-12 does not match that view. Stock vs sheet - pad length 1.45 vs 1.14 (=1.64-0.50); wide-pad centres 4.90/6.50 vs 4.80/6.40; pad centre 1.445 vs 1.07 above the alignment line, a 0.375 mm row offset that lands the contact tails off-centre at the heel; rear shell slot 1.6 pad / 1.2 drill vs the sheet's labelled 1.70/1.40; front shell pad 2.1 vs 2.00. Ruled out as an M-12 vs M-12A variant difference: HRO's base TYPE-C-31-M-12 sheet (C165948, REV A 2020.12.08) carries a dimension-for-dimension IDENTICAL recommended layout, so BOTH vendor sheets disagree with the stock footprint. What IS inherited from the stock part, because it agrees with the sheet exactly, is the datum and the hole PATTERN: alignment holes 5.78 apart, shell slots 8.64 apart and 4.18 front-to-rear, front slot 0.53 above the alignment line, front slot drill 1.70 tall. ALIGNMENT-HOLE DIAMETER IS A DECISION, NOT AN INHERITANCE: sheet nominal 0.60 against a moulded 2-phi 0.50 post (front view). 0.65 is taken - the TOP of the sheet's OWN +/-0.05 band - because these posts are LOCATORS: at the 0.55 bottom of the band a phi 0.50 post has 0.025 mm radial clearance, and a post that will not enter lifts the part off all twelve pads. That failure is far worse than the 0.075 vs 0.050 mm of lateral play 0.65 permits, and final location is set by reflow self-alignment on 12 lands plus 4 soldered legs, not by the posts. SHELL-SLOT WIDTHS (1.00 pad / 0.60 drill) are the one geometry taken from the stock part on trust: the sheet dimensions the slot HEIGHTS and not the widths. A raster read of the sheet at 300 dpi suggests ~1.2 pad / ~0.9 drill, +/-0.1 - an ESTIMATE, so it is recorded here and NOT put into copper; 0.60 already gives about 2x clearance on a ~0.3 mm stamped stainless leg. OPEN, RECORDED NOT HIDDEN: the same raster read puts the two slot CENTRES 4.03 apart (+/-0.08) against the sheet's printed 4.18; 4.18 is a CITED dimension and an estimate does not overrule it, so 4.18 stands - verify against a physical part or a JLC CAD twin before release. PAD NAMES ARE ALPHANUMERIC A1..B12 + SH ON PURPOSE - tscircuit drops the part silently otherwise (ledger S-COUNT, 2026-07-21). The four merged VBUS/GND lands carry TWO coincident pads each so both contact names reach the netlist. Orientation is fixed by the mouth/board edge and by the asymmetric shell slots (front 2.00 tall, rear 1.70), not by a pin-1 mark.")
		(tags "usb usb-c 2.0 receptacle 16P HRO TYPE-C-31-M-12A smt th hybrid")
